WEBVTT

01:32.425 --> 01:34.928
Now, where can we all eat together?

01:36.930 --> 01:37.806
Oh.

01:38.932 --> 01:41.643
The great hall is a mess.

01:41.726 --> 01:43.353
Want me to fix it?

01:43.436 --> 01:44.437
Please.

01:48.274 --> 01:50.777
This'll be a big job.

02:00.829 --> 02:02.747
- It vanished.
- It's pure white.

02:20.014 --> 02:22.392
Now we can have breakfast.

02:23.893 --> 02:25.562
It's back to normal?

02:27.438 --> 02:28.898
What's going on?

02:28.982 --> 02:32.360
Meet my Daemons, Black and White.

02:32.443 --> 02:36.197
This one's name is Whiteout,
and this one's Ink.

02:36.781 --> 02:39.701
I apply Whiteout to anything
I want to fix...

02:39.784 --> 02:42.745
and then write over it with Ink.

02:43.329 --> 02:46.040
They depend on observational
skills and imagination,

02:46.124 --> 02:49.627
so Hagure-sensei's compatibility
with Black and White is excellent.

02:49.711 --> 02:50.670
Sensei?

02:50.753 --> 02:54.507
I'm Hagure Hikaru. I'm a mangaka.

02:55.758 --> 02:59.554
By the way, this spitting they do
is a sign of affection.

03:00.263 --> 03:02.557
What's a mangaka?

03:02.640 --> 03:04.976
Huh? Oh!

03:05.059 --> 03:07.979
I've seen you credited in films
as an original creator!

03:08.062 --> 03:12.191
Thankfully, I make a decent living.

03:12.692 --> 03:14.485
Hagure is my pen name.

03:14.569 --> 03:16.821
My real name is Kagemori Hikaru.

03:17.405 --> 03:18.489
Pen name?

03:18.573 --> 03:19.616
A writer's alias.

03:19.699 --> 03:23.536
Our family does some ruthless stuff,

03:23.620 --> 03:26.706
so I use a pen name
to avoid controversy over my identity.

03:26.789 --> 03:28.958
So you're a Kagemori, huh?

03:29.542 --> 03:31.753
We're brothers.

03:32.337 --> 03:33.421
I'm Hikaru, the oldest.

03:33.504 --> 03:35.256
Asuma, the middle brother.

03:35.840 --> 03:38.092
I'm Jin, the youngest.

03:38.176 --> 03:40.178
The youngest?

03:40.261 --> 03:42.263
You're the youngest of the three?

03:42.847 --> 03:43.765
Is there a problem?

03:43.848 --> 03:48.186
That said, we all have different mothers.

03:49.270 --> 03:50.271
We look nothing alike, right?

03:50.855 --> 03:54.359
As the oldest, Hagure-kun
is the next head of the clan.

03:54.442 --> 03:56.653
You'll benefit from cultivating
a friendship with him.

03:56.736 --> 04:00.531
No way! I can't take
over this sketchy clan!

04:00.615 --> 04:05.036
I want to live a peaceful life,
happily drawing my manga!

04:05.119 --> 04:08.957
Unlike you guys, I still have
a decent set of morals!

04:09.540 --> 04:14.337
I heard crazy creators write
more interesting stories.

04:14.420 --> 04:16.214
That sounds like a stereotype.

04:16.297 --> 04:22.512
Mr. Mangaka, the parts you
fixed are monochrome.

04:22.595 --> 04:24.222
Is this safe?

04:24.305 --> 04:25.932
It's totally fine.

04:26.015 --> 04:31.562
The surrounding colors will eventually
bleed into it until it's back to normal.

04:32.522 --> 04:34.899
I messed up the details on the pillar.

04:34.983 --> 04:36.651
I made it too clean.

04:36.734 --> 04:41.614
Judging by the building's age,
the edges should be smoother.

04:41.698 --> 04:43.241
I made them too sharp.

04:43.324 --> 04:44.951
I screwed up the tatami, too.

04:45.034 --> 04:49.664
Mats that see a lot of traffic
should be more damaged.

04:49.747 --> 04:53.918
These look brand new and sterile.

04:54.752 --> 04:57.338
I'm fixing it!

04:59.424 --> 05:01.843
Let's have breakfast first.

05:05.013 --> 05:06.597
Thank you for waiting.

05:06.681 --> 05:10.935
Seating order... doesn't matter, I suppose.

05:11.019 --> 05:12.478
Sit wherever you want.

05:13.229 --> 05:15.231
We're an upstart clan.

05:15.315 --> 05:19.819
Don't worry about seating order,
traditions, or etiquette.

05:19.902 --> 05:21.487
- One, two!
- Three, four!

05:21.571 --> 05:23.156
- One, two!
- Three, four!

05:23.239 --> 05:24.657
- One, two!
- Three, four!

05:24.741 --> 05:26.409
- One, two!
- Three, four!

05:26.492 --> 05:27.994
- One, two!
- Three, four!

05:29.662 --> 05:31.748
- One, two!
- Three, four!

05:31.831 --> 05:33.166
- One, two!
- Three, four!

05:33.249 --> 05:34.917
- One, two!
- Three, four!

05:35.001 --> 05:36.002
Have a seat.

05:36.085 --> 05:37.837
Uh, thank you.

05:41.007 --> 05:42.675
- One, two!
- Three, four!

05:42.759 --> 05:44.093
- One, two!
- Three, four!

05:44.177 --> 05:45.011
- What's this?
- One, two!

05:45.094 --> 05:47.889
- We get seats, too?
- Three, four!

05:47.972 --> 05:50.308
We don't eat human food.

05:50.892 --> 05:52.560
You're guests.

05:52.643 --> 05:55.063
We treat all guests equally.

06:03.905 --> 06:08.284
So, how did you learn
Mr. Big Brother was here?

06:08.367 --> 06:09.952
That's a secret.

06:12.288 --> 06:16.250
The mansion was attacked
by multiple Daemons last night.

06:17.126 --> 06:20.088
Didn't your Higashi Village send them?

06:20.171 --> 06:22.131
What? Don't ask me.

06:22.215 --> 06:25.635
He instantly killed our
delightful breakfast vibes!

06:26.219 --> 06:29.764
Why would I attack Kagemori headquarters?

06:30.389 --> 06:35.019
It happened right after Mr. Big Brother
arrived. The timing's too perfect.

06:35.520 --> 06:36.521
So good!

06:37.021 --> 06:39.524
Brother's eating...

06:40.149 --> 06:45.363
I hear Tadera clan members
can slip through barriers.

06:45.863 --> 06:48.616
I don't know how to pass through
other clans' barriers.

06:48.699 --> 06:52.036
Brother's drinking miso soup...

06:52.120 --> 06:53.371
So good!

06:53.454 --> 06:56.874
Anyway, Asa-chan,
have the Kagemoris been mistreating you?

06:57.458 --> 06:59.043
Don't worry.

06:59.127 --> 07:02.547
They've fed and raised me well.

07:03.131 --> 07:04.257
This mansion is safe.

07:04.340 --> 07:07.468
I don't get attacked by assassins here.

07:07.969 --> 07:10.555
Though they did get in last night.

07:10.638 --> 07:13.891
Take one step outside the mansion,
and you're surrounded by enemies.

07:13.975 --> 07:17.061
I don't really want her
leaving the mansion,

07:17.145 --> 07:22.066
but when our infirmary's insufficient,
she has to go visit regular hospitals.

07:22.817 --> 07:26.904
Security is inevitably weaker there.

07:26.988 --> 07:29.991
I was captured by Higashi
Village assassins

07:30.074 --> 07:32.785
when I was at a hospital
outside the mansion.

07:33.369 --> 07:35.872
Were you seriously ill with something?

07:36.873 --> 07:38.624
A gastric ulcer.

07:39.333 --> 07:44.005
The stress from constantly being
targeted by Higashi Village agents

07:44.088 --> 07:46.257
put a hole in my stomach.

07:46.340 --> 07:48.551
Don't blame me.

07:48.634 --> 07:50.678
I wasn't the one giving the orders.

07:50.761 --> 07:56.934
Also, regular people are at hospitals,
so it's a huge nuisance for everyone.

07:57.018 --> 07:58.603
Please stop doing that.

07:59.187 --> 08:01.647
Like I said, it wasn't me.

08:01.731 --> 08:06.444
Sorry about the Higashi
Village extremists.

08:06.527 --> 08:11.157
Oh, what does your family
register look like, Asa-chan?

08:11.240 --> 08:15.244
It's a pain to use general hospitals
without an insurance card.

08:15.912 --> 08:17.997
I'm wondering what to do about Yuru.

08:18.498 --> 08:21.083
I still don't have a register down here.

08:21.584 --> 08:23.461
That can't be easy.

08:24.045 --> 08:26.631
Since my mother's originally from here,

08:26.714 --> 08:29.842
I thought about getting
a register that way.

08:31.177 --> 08:36.182
But she went missing with Father
after someone attacked her.

08:36.265 --> 08:39.477
What? Your parents are missing?

08:39.560 --> 08:40.686
Apparently.

08:41.729 --> 08:44.982
I know I'm on Higashi Village's side,

08:45.566 --> 08:48.861
but I've never heard
about your parents going missing.

08:48.945 --> 08:49.862
At the very least,

08:49.946 --> 08:54.283
I don't think it was done
by the Higashi Village community I know.

08:54.909 --> 08:58.538
And you expect us to believe you?

08:59.205 --> 09:05.419
I'll kill anyone who enters our territory,
but I never attack anyone.

09:05.503 --> 09:08.839
I don't agree
with the Higashi Village extremists.

09:09.840 --> 09:15.012
I came here unarmed and peacefully
today to pick up Yuru.

09:15.096 --> 09:18.933
Are you sure it wasn't Kagemori
extremists who did it?

09:19.517 --> 09:24.522
I've heard you're not a monolith either.

09:25.856 --> 09:31.320
What does the Kagemori clan head
ultimately want to do with the twins?

09:35.783 --> 09:39.704
Every time the ill-fated twins are born,
the world is thrown into chaos.

09:40.913 --> 09:43.708
We're better off without Break or Seal.

09:46.794 --> 09:50.673
It's best for Asa and Yuru-kun
to be the final set of twins

09:50.756 --> 09:55.219
and to get rid of Higashi Village
that produces them.

09:56.178 --> 09:59.390
It's a miserable village
bound by outdated values

09:59.473 --> 10:02.977
that can't give up its dreams
of conquering the world.

10:03.811 --> 10:05.646
Times have changed.

10:05.730 --> 10:08.441
We share their blood.

10:08.524 --> 10:10.985
It's our responsibility
to put them to rest.

10:11.819 --> 10:13.654
I disagree.

10:14.447 --> 10:20.411
Those chosen to wield power should use
that power to peacefully govern the world.

10:20.995 --> 10:23.414
That's their responsibility.

10:23.914 --> 10:27.251
After all, they were granted
that power by the gods.

10:27.335 --> 10:31.505
And the Kagemori clan has
what it takes to control that power?

10:31.589 --> 10:36.636
Yes. The village that produces the powers
of Break and Seal can continue to exist.

10:37.428 --> 10:40.056
We shouldn't deny their very existence.

10:40.139 --> 10:43.851
However, they should exist under
the control of a suitable organization.

10:43.934 --> 10:45.895
That's what I believe.

10:48.898 --> 10:49.732
Right and Left.

10:50.358 --> 10:51.275
Yes?

10:51.901 --> 10:57.907
When I asked if we're cursed children
who cause chaos, you instantly denied it.

10:58.783 --> 11:03.746
You said it's the people who want
to use our power who start the fighting.

11:04.330 --> 11:10.753
I found solace in your instant denial
that we're at fault.

11:12.380 --> 11:15.216
You made me feel like it's fine
for us to live.

11:19.095 --> 11:20.221
Thank you.

11:28.687 --> 11:30.314
Thanks for the meal.

11:32.691 --> 11:35.486
She apologizes for everything.

11:36.153 --> 11:39.031
I won't forgive her
for attacking the village,

11:39.115 --> 11:41.575
but she apologies for things
that aren't her fault.

11:42.493 --> 11:46.580
Who's making her feel
so ashamed of herself?

11:47.164 --> 11:50.334
Who's making her think
everything is her fault?

11:51.252 --> 11:56.424
Why do we have to live in secret
just because we're destined twins?

11:57.425 --> 12:00.970
Why do others get to dictate how we live?

12:06.308 --> 12:09.145
If the Kagemori clan isn't a monolith,

12:09.228 --> 12:13.524
then the extremists will probably
hear about this conversation, too.

12:14.692 --> 12:20.614
Dera-san, make sure Higashi Village hears
what I'm about to say, too.

12:22.199 --> 12:24.577
I won't run or hide.

12:24.660 --> 12:26.579
I don't have a reason to sneak around.

12:27.246 --> 12:30.458
I don't care if you're from Higashi
Village or the Kagemori clan.

12:30.541 --> 12:34.170
If you want my head, come and get it.

12:35.212 --> 12:36.088
But...

12:36.964 --> 12:41.927
once I defeat my attackers, I'll squeeze
them for all the information I can.

12:42.428 --> 12:44.513
Listen, Yuru...

12:45.598 --> 12:47.933
Brother, you big idiot!

12:51.937 --> 12:54.690
Brother, you big idiot!

13:01.280 --> 13:03.491
Why are you calling me an idiot?

13:03.574 --> 13:05.034
"I won't run or hide"?

13:05.117 --> 13:06.785
You can't be serious!

13:07.453 --> 13:09.914
You're only saying that
because you don't know

13:09.997 --> 13:13.709
how hard it is to be constantly
targeted by assassins.

13:14.543 --> 13:17.213
I don't want you to suffer
the same fate I did.

13:17.296 --> 13:19.340
You should run. You should hide.

13:19.423 --> 13:21.258
Don't throw your life away!

13:21.842 --> 13:26.263
Is Yuru-kun the type to attack
aggressively on his turns?

13:26.347 --> 13:27.598
Mostly, yes.

13:27.681 --> 13:29.600
Right and Left, say something to—

13:30.226 --> 13:34.897
As his Daemons, we have to do as he says.

13:34.980 --> 13:37.525
We can't help whatever trouble
happens to cross our path.

13:38.025 --> 13:40.361
You two seem really happy about this.

13:40.444 --> 13:42.488
What's the problem?

13:42.571 --> 13:48.494
Your brother's offering to take on half
the burden you've been carrying alone.

13:48.577 --> 13:49.620
Gabby-chan!

13:50.204 --> 13:53.499
- Our master is a kind man.
- What?

13:55.459 --> 14:00.172
Well, yeah. I already know he is.

14:03.676 --> 14:09.181
Yuru-kun, is joining the Kagemori clan
not an option for you?

14:09.265 --> 14:15.104
You'll be safer here, and we'll
make sure you're comfortable.

14:15.187 --> 14:16.105
What do you say?

14:16.188 --> 14:17.231
No.

14:17.314 --> 14:18.482
That was quick.

14:19.066 --> 14:23.320
You called Higashi Village miserable,

14:23.404 --> 14:25.447
but that's where I was born and raised.

14:25.948 --> 14:27.074
I have friends there.

14:28.325 --> 14:33.497
I understand your ideals,
but that's different from accepting them.

14:34.456 --> 14:38.043
I'll never side with someone
who did that to my village.

14:39.169 --> 14:43.924
I appreciate you looking for our parents,
but I'll do things my way.

14:45.467 --> 14:50.097
For now, I'll work with Dera-san
to look for them.

14:51.724 --> 14:56.186
Honestly, I wish you'd lie low, too.

14:56.937 --> 14:59.690
I'm technically his guardian.

14:59.773 --> 15:04.111
All I can do is respect
how he wants to live and protect him.

15:04.653 --> 15:10.200
So, can we go now,
Kagemori-san and Asa-chan?

15:13.162 --> 15:15.831
Divine Guardians Right and Left. Dera-san.

15:21.170 --> 15:24.632
Please look after my brother.

15:25.633 --> 15:26.884
As you wish.

15:28.218 --> 15:29.553
I'll do my best.

15:40.064 --> 15:42.191
This is as far as I can go.

15:42.691 --> 15:44.485
That's the edge of the barrier.

15:45.277 --> 15:49.406
I could be attacked by people trying
to get Break the second I step outside.

15:50.574 --> 15:52.242
Be careful, Brother.

15:58.707 --> 16:02.461
She can't freely exit these gates.

16:03.963 --> 16:09.051
All she did was replace that room
with this mansion.

16:09.969 --> 16:13.597
Oh, right. I want to show you something.

16:14.348 --> 16:15.724
Look.

16:15.808 --> 16:17.851
Huh? What?

16:18.560 --> 16:20.270
Father and Mother?

16:20.354 --> 16:22.690
This is them
right before they went missing.

16:23.399 --> 16:25.526
What is this? A woodblock print?

16:26.485 --> 16:29.530
I guess it's like a really
amazing woodblock print.

16:30.781 --> 16:33.367
Okay, Brother, look up here.

16:36.787 --> 16:40.791
This technology perfectly
captures a moment.

16:41.375 --> 16:46.296
I don't get it, but I'm really impressed!

16:46.380 --> 16:50.551
I successfully took advantage of the
situation to get a photo of my brother.

16:51.135 --> 16:52.302
That's amazing!

16:52.386 --> 16:55.264
We want a picture with Yuru, too!

16:55.347 --> 16:57.016
Unfortunately...

16:58.600 --> 17:01.020
Daemons don't show up in photos.

17:01.687 --> 17:03.981
They're like spirits, after all.

17:04.064 --> 17:08.193
Very rarely, Daemons do show
up if the timing's right.

17:08.986 --> 17:10.863
You see it on ghost shows sometimes.

17:11.363 --> 17:12.322
Asa.

17:13.532 --> 17:16.118
Let me see Father and Mother again.

17:21.832 --> 17:23.459
They're wearing clothes from down here.

17:24.626 --> 17:26.420
They look so strange.

17:26.920 --> 17:29.256
I haven't seen them in ten years.

17:30.215 --> 17:32.176
I wonder where they are now.

17:33.135 --> 17:36.388
I'm sure they're alive and well.

17:37.514 --> 17:39.516
I'll have this printed and send it to you.

17:40.100 --> 17:41.268
I can have this?

17:41.852 --> 17:44.271
Where do you live now?

17:44.354 --> 17:45.856
What's your address?

17:45.939 --> 17:49.109
Where do I live? Uh...

17:49.860 --> 17:50.986
Guntama Prefecture?

17:51.070 --> 17:51.987
Where?

17:52.071 --> 17:56.742
I failed to take advantage of the
situation to get my brother's address.

17:57.326 --> 17:58.535
Dera-san, where is your place?

17:58.619 --> 18:02.331
I can't give my address to someone
working with the Kagemoris.

18:02.956 --> 18:05.626
We'd like to notify Mr. Big Brother
if there are any developments

18:05.709 --> 18:07.336
regarding his parents.

18:07.920 --> 18:09.797
We won't ask for your address,

18:09.880 --> 18:12.216
but if we could at least get an
email address or phone number...

18:12.299 --> 18:13.342
Hell no.

18:13.425 --> 18:17.721
I don't want you finding me over
some little bit of personal information.

18:19.139 --> 18:24.311
That said, I agree that it'd be nice
to have some way to contact each other.

18:24.394 --> 18:25.938
Carrier pigeons?

18:26.021 --> 18:27.272
Radio?

18:27.940 --> 18:29.817
The message board at Shinjuku Station?

18:29.900 --> 18:30.818
Smoke signals.

18:30.901 --> 18:33.153
That's a fire law violation.

18:34.780 --> 18:37.699
In that case, come here
if you need anything.

18:38.992 --> 18:40.536
A girls bar?

18:40.619 --> 18:42.830
It's one of the Kagemori
clan's businesses.

18:43.497 --> 18:47.668
They should accommodate you
if you mention my name.

18:48.168 --> 18:49.837
Use that business to contact us.

18:52.422 --> 18:54.174
Sure thing.

18:54.258 --> 18:57.177
That face says,
"I'm drinking there on your tab."

18:58.178 --> 19:01.265
Well, thanks for looking
for the twins' parents.

19:01.348 --> 19:03.851
And thanks for breakfast.

19:07.563 --> 19:08.397
Brother.

19:11.066 --> 19:17.114
Father and Mother were heartbroken
they couldn't take you with us.

19:17.614 --> 19:20.868
Granny Yamaha got in their way.

19:20.951 --> 19:24.746
It was all they could do to leave
the mountain with just me.

19:25.873 --> 19:28.250
They wanted to take you too.

19:28.333 --> 19:31.628
They didn't leave you behind
because they wanted to.

19:44.516 --> 19:48.437
Just hearing that made
it worth coming here.

19:52.107 --> 19:53.150
See you later.

20:15.797 --> 20:19.176
Brother, take care of yourself.

20:22.262 --> 20:23.555
See you later.

20:34.316 --> 20:35.943
Hey, Yuru?

20:36.026 --> 20:38.987
I was careless! She snuck up on me!

20:39.071 --> 20:41.949
If she were a bear, I'd be dead!

20:42.032 --> 20:43.659
Are you for real?

20:45.744 --> 20:47.079
There's no doubt about it.

20:47.704 --> 20:49.665
That's Asa.

20:50.666 --> 20:51.959
Brother.

20:52.793 --> 20:55.003
Take care of yourself.

20:59.216 --> 21:01.677
That's definitely her.

21:01.760 --> 21:05.889
She's definitely my actual sister.

21:08.392 --> 21:10.769
Why? Damn it.

21:15.565 --> 21:19.653
Jin-san, don't put a tail on them.

21:19.736 --> 21:20.904
Trust is important.

21:22.531 --> 21:23.740
You're right.

21:25.409 --> 21:29.037
Normally, a third party should command

21:29.121 --> 21:33.000
Right and Left to control Break and Seal.

21:33.500 --> 21:37.921
But they just had to be acquired

21:38.005 --> 21:41.508
by the twin with the power of Seal.

21:42.175 --> 21:46.138
There will be no one to stop them
if something happens to Yuru.

21:48.390 --> 21:52.644
There's no telling what could happen.

23:27.614 --> 23:28.907
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

23:32.494 --> 23:33.995
Are they Kagemoris?

23:34.079 --> 23:35.247
We're being followed.

23:35.831 --> 23:37.916
You'll work like horses.

23:37.999 --> 23:40.919
Subtitle translation by: Sho Stifler
